Upstream licence note — readout_genesis import (Toledo, 2026-09-06)
====================================================================

Source: public repository at commit 082dde893b70c7500c13d463239909c99cf17f0a
(anchored in registry/coq_imports.json and coq/readout_genesis/PROVENANCE.json;
this repository is one of the five public Coq import sources per the Toledo
design meeting, T8, docs/MEETING_2026-09-06_toledo_design.md).

Readout-not-truth check performed at import time (2026-09-06), directly
against the checked-out working tree at the anchored commit:

  - No `LICENSE` / `LICENSE.md` / `LICENCE*` file exists anywhere in the
    repository (checked with `find . -iname 'LICENSE*'`, excluding `.git/`).
  - `README.md` and `CITATION.cff` were grepped for the words
    "license"/"licence" (case-insensitive): no match in either file.

There is therefore no upstream licence text to reproduce verbatim here.
This file records that finding rather than fabricating a licence. The
39 `.v` files copied into this directory (`coq/readout_genesis/formal/` and
`coq/readout_genesis/domains/standard_model/`) are imported under the
Toledo project's own general public-source import policy (T8): they are
public GitHub source, copied byte-for-byte (verified: zero diff against
the upstream working tree at the anchored commit), with provenance
(commit + blob per file) recorded in `PROVENANCE.json`.

If the source repository's owner (Yaoharee Lahtee / ANSE.ASIA) later adds
an explicit licence file upstream, this note should be revisited and, if
appropriate, replaced with the actual licence text at that time.
